#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Make the check suite runnable before a session forms any belief about repo health.
#
# WHY A HOOK AND NOT PROSE, which is this settings file's own stated rationale: an agent
# must CHOOSE to read prose, and attention degrades as context fills. A hook fires on
# every session regardless of what anyone read or remembers.
#
# WHAT IT PREVENTS, measured on origin/main at d6ef7e9 on 2026-08-25:
#   without pydantic:  5 BLOCKING failures, 10 advisory   -> RESULT: FAIL
#   with pydantic:     0 blocking,           4 advisory   -> PASS, 50 green
# The five were validate_schema, validate_evidence_state, audit_adversarial_use,
# decision_capture and doctrine_recheck -- the entire governance battery. A session
# without them sees a red repository it did not break, and CLAUDE.md tells it to
# reproduce a red check before assuming it is theirs. That advice INVERTS here: the
# reproduction succeeds, on main, and the wrong conclusion is available.
#
# THE DEPENDENCY LIST HAS ONE HOME: governance/check-registry.yaml, whose `batteries:`
# block declares `deps:` per battery. requirements.txt is a SECOND home and it already
# disagreed -- it names pydantic and PyYAML and omits jsonschema, which the registry
# declares for the `research` battery and which attestation validation needs. Found on
# 2026-08-25 by an attestation validation failing on a fresh container. Read the registry
# (rule 5: point, do not copy); fall back to a literal list only if it cannot be parsed.
#
# NEVER `pip install -r requirements.txt` IN THIS CONTAINER. It pins PyYAML==6.0.3, and
# pip refuses to uninstall the Debian-managed PyYAML 6.0.1 that is already present and
# already works: "Cannot uninstall PyYAML 6.0.1, RECORD file not found." The whole install
# then aborts and nothing lands. Install the individual packages.
#
# Exits 0 unconditionally. A dependency installer must never be the thing that stops a
# session starting -- offline, no pip, no network are all survivable; the checks stay red
# and say why.

cd "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}" 2>/dev/null || true

DEPS=$(python3 - <<'PY' 2>/dev/null
try:
    import yaml
    d = yaml.safe_load(open("governance/check-registry.yaml"))
    out = set()
    for b in (d.get("batteries") or {}).values():
----
{
  "_comment": [
    "Harness-level enforcement of the research contract. Per owner directive 2026-07-24:",
    "'OUR RESEARCH IS INVALID IF IT IS NOT COMPLIANT WITH OUR GOVERNANCE AND VERIFICATION",
    "TOOLS AND RULES AND ETHOS.'",
    "",
    "WHY HOOKS AND NOT PROSE: the 2026-07-24 research run skipped Co-1, citation mining, clause",
    "citation and combinatorial pairing while the rules for all four sat documented in skills/,",
    "governance/ and CLAUDE.md. The rules did not fail; PROSE failed — an agent must choose to",
    "load it, and attention degrades as context fills. Hooks run at the HARNESS level: they fire",
    "on every session regardless of what any agent has read or remembers.",
    "",
    "SessionStart re-injects the contract at the top of every session (before context fills).",
    "Stop runs the mechanical definition-of-done gate so a session cannot quietly end",
    "non-compliant. Neither blocks work; both make non-compliance impossible to not-see."
  ],
  "_permissions_comment": [
    "scripts/migrate_db.py is the ONLY sanctioned writer of data/guidebook.db (CLAUDE.md",
    "rule 3: 'Never write data/guidebook.db directly. Migrations only.'). Every research",
    "batch ends there — scratch copy -> db.py -> emit_batch_sql.py -> emit_data_migration.py",
    "-> migrate_db.py — so without this rule no batch, and no ratification, can land.",
    "",
    "It is allowed rather than prompted because the script is itself the safety mechanism:",
    "it applies migrations forward-only inside one transaction, stamps user_version and the",
    "data_migrations ledger atomically with the DDL, and rolls back as a unit on failure.",
    "Blanket shell access is NOT granted — the two rules below name one script and nothing",
    "else."
  ],
  "_deny_comment": [
    "CLAUDE.md rule 9 (owner instruction 2026-09-23): do not watch PRs; open the PR last.",
    "Most PR-activity wake-ups in the 2026-09 transcripts were CI reporting green on a",
    "subscribed PR; each cost a full-context turn that did no work. Denying the tools is",
    "what makes the rule hold. Both subscribe tools are named because sessions used both.",
    "send_later and create_trigger are denied because they were used to poll CI; the deny",
    "cannot tell a poll from any other reminder, so lift it when a reminder is wanted."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(python3 scripts/migrate_db.py)",
      "Bash(python3 scripts/migrate_db.py *)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "mcp__github__subscribe_pr_activity",
      "mcp__Claude_Code_Remote__subscribe_pr_activity",
      "mcp__Claude_Code_Remote__send_later",
      "mcp__Claude_Code_Remote__create_trigger"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/.claude/hooks/record-command.py\" 2>/dev/null || true",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "WebSearch|WebFetch",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/.claude/hooks/record-command.py\" 2>/dev/null || true",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "printf '%s\\n' '================ GUIDEBOOK RESEARCH CONTRACT (harness-injected) ================' 'RESEARCH IS INVALID IF NOT COMPLIANT WITH OUR GOVERNANCE, VERIFICATION TOOLS,' 'RULES AND ETHOS. Compliance is mechanical, not remembered.' '' 'BEFORE admitting evidence:' '  R1  Co-1 / T2 / Co-2 pass FIRST - no exceptions (Co-1 co-primary w/ T1, CRPD' '      4.3)' '  R5  Non-English peer-reviewed work is ACADEMIC, not grey. Non-indexation in' '      PubMed/Scopus is an INDEXING fact, not an evidence-quality fact.' '  R9  Pre-check the DOI. If it exists, cross-file the existing ref_id - never' '      duplicate.' '  R10 Re-retrieve every locator. DOI -> Crossref/PubMed -> publisher ->' '      repository. A publisher block is NOT a terminal answer. No re-retrieval' '      = no admission. NEVER leave verification_status NULL on a source' '      carrying a URL: that is the exact pool the scheduled url-verification' '      cron claims, and it pushes a DB blob to main. UNVERIFIED is a real value' '      - say it.' '  R17 Every admission has a logged search behind it. A source taken from a' '      list is logged as one (db.py log-search --origin lead-index ...' '      --admitted-ref-id R), so search coverage sees it; a held source with no' '      edge gets one (db.py link-admission).' '' 'WHILE searching:' '  R2  Mine every CONFIRMED T1-T2 anchor backward AND forward. Depth 2-3 via' '      citation-miner; gap-driven mode is depth-1 per pass and hands off.' '  R4  Cross slug x EVERY lens: identity / access-need / ICF (D-0170, the' '      medical lens deleted by the owner 2026-11-16). NOT (item x population) -' '      the item layer was deleted 2026-09-01, and base_taxonomy_identity is' '      ONLY the identity lens, so framing on it alone is the traversal D-0184' '      rejected. THE KEY IS RULED: a cell is parameter_id (base_parameters) x' '      at least one of the three lens columns - subject ruled 2026-08-26, lens' '      ruled 2026-08-28 as relaxed by D-0182.' '  R7  Capture FAILURE / HARM / INADEQUACY as first-class evidence, not a' '      by-product.' '  R8  Log EVERY query verbatim before screening, WITH --prior-expectation' '      written BEFORE you run it - a prior recorded after seeing results is a' '      rationalisation, not a prior (DR-2026-05-09). KEEP EMPTIES - a' '      zero-yield search is a COMPLETED unit of work. Never delete or backfill' '      them.' '  R13 Grade population-of-STUDY vs population-SERVED on every admission. No' '      match row = silently claiming they are the same.' '      Children/general-population/no-participants = PROXY.' '  R14 A zero-yield search is evidence of ABSENCE only if the query was' '      well-formed. PubMed AND-chains every term: say query-shape failure vs' '      wrong index vs genuine absence.' '' 'WHEN filing:' '  R3  Quantified values need a locator or [UNVERIFIED-QUANT]. Code/standard' '      values: clause/section/page. Outcome claims: DOI + page/table, or a' '      direct URL.' '  R6  Findings go in findings_note. deferred_reason means DELIBERATELY NOT' '      SEARCHED.' '  R7  Off-slug or unverified material -> search_candidates' '      (REHOME/MISC/PENDING), not prose.' '  R11 No back-translation. Every alias carries its in-language source, else' '      [UNVERIFIED-TERMS]. HARVEST AS YOU GO: db.py observe-term for each' '      concept phrase a source USES, in the source'\\''s own words. That is a fact' '      about the document, not a claim it names one of our categories; judgment' '      adjudicates it later (D-0173).' '  R12 Case studies -> case_studies. Economics -> economics_entries. Code' '      values -> research_code_leads. Never leave them in prose notes.' '  R15 A staged candidate description is a HYPOTHESIS. On resolution,' '      re-describe it from the source and CORRECT it if you over-claimed. Do' '      not let your own guess harden into fact.' '  R16 A figure a source states is extracted against a parameter, never left' '      only in prose or a code lead (a lead records where to look; R12 keeps' '      it): observe-term -> adjudicate-term (or add-term) -> add-parameter ->' '      add-extraction. Every phrase observed on this batch'\\''s admissions is' '      adjudicated (NOT-OURS and DEFERRED are answers), and every term those' '      adjudications name is a parameter or is declined with its reason (db.py' '      decline-parameter). Read EVERY admission against the WHOLE parameter' '      list, whatever slug it came in under, and record the reading (db.py' '      record-scan --mode catalogue): slugs guide searches, not what is mined' '      from a source.' '' 'ALWAYS: migrations-only (emit_data_migration -> migrate_db). Never hand-edit the DB.' 'Never author best_practice_synthesis below the Opus floor. Never move an adjudicated figure.' 'Gate before you claim done:  python3 scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py --session <id>' '==============================================================================='"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/.claude/hooks/ensure-deps.sh\" 2>&1 || true",
            "timeout": 120
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/scripts/fix_stop_hook_loop.sh\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "if [ -f scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py ] && [ -f data/guidebook.db ]; then out=$(python3 scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py --all 2>&1); rc=$?; printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | tail -n 20; if [ \"$rc\" -eq 0 ]; then echo \"RESEARCH DoD: PASS (exit 0)\"; else echo \"RESEARCH DoD: FAIL (exit $rc) — non-blocking by design, but this session closed non-compliant. See governance/research-contract.yaml.\"; fi; fi"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}/scripts/preserve_transcripts.py\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true"
